{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he shall assess.</b> That the one assessed is set in a single row with such-and-such, and his like — there is none compared to you. And the word העריך is from the intensive reflexive binyan, and likewise יעריכנו הכהן, to distinguish between it and יערכנו לפני ה׳." "<b>And the priest shall set him.</b> As if it said: and the priest shall set him before the priest, as I explained. And [this is analogous to] ויצק על כף הכהן השמאלית, and it would be a way of elegance. Or והעמידו may mean that the one vowing sets himself."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:57.150371968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}